    <string name="privacy_summary">The app collects nothing, sends nothing and has no internet access. There are no accounts, ads or analytics, and no history of the tags you read is kept.\n\nText written to a tag is stored on the tag itself in the standard NFC format, so anyone with an NFC phone can read it. Do not put secrets on a tag.\n\nVoice notes are recorded only when you press Record voice note. They are stored only inside the app and never included in cloud backups. Exported ZIP files are saved where you choose.\n\nDictation uses your phone\'s speech recognition service, and reading aloud uses the voice you choose in Settings. These services, often from Google, process the audio or text under their own privacy policies.\n\nLinks, phone numbers, Wi-Fi networks and other content from tags are only shown. Another app opens only when you press its button.</string>
